[$in title:["Plain Markdown"]]
[$in description:["Plain Markdown content dependencies for HTML projects."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
[section, $md:
    # Plain Markdown

    A `.md` file remains ordinary Markdown. The compiler renders it at compile
    time and exports the HTML as `content`, but it never interprets Moth syntax
    inside the file.

    This keeps plain content portable across Markdown tools. Choose `.mtf` only
    when content needs Moth constants, templates or `@html` helpers.
]

